# Git commits

Inspired by [awesome-cursorrules git-conventional-commit-messages.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules/blob/main/rules/git-conventional-commit-messages.mdc), adapted to this repo's history.

## Message style

- Match recent commits: short imperative English summary (e.g. `Add …`, `Fix …`, `Use …`)
- Conventional types (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, …) are optional, not required
- Focus on why when it is not obvious from the diff
- Only commit when the user explicitly asks

## After commit

Run `./scripts/cleanup-artifacts.sh` (also via `.git/hooks/post-commit`).

## README on GitHub commits

When the user asks to commit and README is part of the change, keep:

1. Код подготовлен с помощью Cursor
2. Донат https://www.donationalerts.com/r/themarfa
